<title>USA: Hershey sees $0.29/shr loss on sale of Euro units.</title>
<headline>Hershey sees $0.29/shr loss on sale of Euro units.</headline>
<dateline>HERSHEY, Pa. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hershey Foods Corp on Tuesday estimated it would see a loss of $45 million, or $0.29 per share, on the disposal of its two European confectionary interests.</p>
<p>Earlier, Hershey said it would sell Gubor Schokoladen, its German praline maker, and Sperlari, its Italian sugar confectionary company, to Huhtamaki Oy, the international foods company based in Finland.</p>
<p>Huhtamaki will pay $110 for the Hershey interests.</p>
<p>The transaction is expected to be completed by the end of this year, Hershey said.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk +1 212 859 1610</p>
